# SportLynk ML service — environment contract
#
# COPY THIS FILE to `.env` in the same directory and fill in ML_API_KEY.
# `.env` is gitignored (root .gitignore: `**/*.env`) and must stay that way.
#
#   cd ml-service
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ML_API_KEY  (REQUIRED — the service refuses to start without it)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The shared secret between this service and the Node backend. It must be
# BYTE-IDENTICAL to ML_API_KEY in backend/.env — no trailing space, no quotes, no
# newline difference. If they differ, every call from Node answers 401 and the
# dashboard silently serves heuristic prices, which looks exactly like the model
# not being trained yet.
#
# To check without printing either secret, compare the fingerprints:
#   ml-service:  curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health     -> data.apiKeyFingerprint
#   backend:     node src/scripts/check_ml_service.js  -> prints the same digest
# Equal fingerprints mean equal keys.
#
# Minimum 16 characters; 64 hex chars (32 bytes) is what the command above gives.
ML_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — the defaults below are what app/core/config.py already uses
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bind address. 127.0.0.1 means nothing outside this machine can reach the
# service. Do NOT change it to 0.0.0.0 on a laptop or a shared network: this
# process has no user model, no JWT and no rate limiting — its only protection is
# the API key and the fact that it is not reachable. (Render sets its own PORT and
# requires 0.0.0.0; that is handled at deploy time in S.7, where the service sits
# behind Render's TLS and the key is a real secret.)
# ML_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ML_PORT=8000

# trace | debug | info | warning | error
# ML_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Where artifacts, generated CSVs and reports live. Defaults are the ml-service/
# subdirectories of the same name; override only if you keep large artifacts
# outside the repo.
# ML_MODEL_DIR=
# ML_DATA_DIR=
# ML_REPORT_DIR=
# The SAME value as backend/.env RECO_EXPORT_API_KEY (byte-identical). build_reco.py
# sends it as the X-Reco-Export-Key header to pull the read-only training snapshot.
# Generate once (either side):  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
RECO_EXPORT_API_KEY=
RECO_EXPORT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/internal/export/reco-data
